@article{1005.93044,
	Abstract = {{The authors study finite-dimensional, nonlinear systems of the
    form $$\dot x= f(x,u,w),\quad y= h(x),$$ where $u$ denotes a
    control input, and $w$ denotes a disturbance which takes value
    on a compact convex set. The main result states that the following
    three facts are equivalent.\par
1) Uniform input-output-to-state
    stability (UIOSS). It means that the norm of the state variable
    can be majorized at every instant $t$ by suitable functions of
    the initial state, of the past control and of the past output.
    This is interpreted as a detectability property.\par
2) Existence
    of a positive definite, proper function $V$ solving an appropriate
    dissipation inequality (characterization in terms of Lyapunov
    functions).\par
3) Existence of a state norm-estimator (observer).\par
The
    paper deals with other related properties such as integral-to-integral
    IOSS and global asymptotic stability modulo output.}},
